{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-12983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation $4{z}^{2}+4z=12$ can be written in the form $(z+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-12983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, divide it by the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{z}^{2}+4z & =12 \\\\ 4({z}^{2}+z) & =12 \\\\ {z}^{2}+z & =3 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot z & =3 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot z+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {(z+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(z+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {(z+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{12}{4} \\\\ {(z+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{13}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=\\frac{1}{2},q=\\frac{13}{4},$ and $p+q=\\frac{15}{4}.$ \n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(z+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{4}} \\\\ |z+\\frac{1}{2}| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2} \\\\ z+\\frac{1}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2} \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2} \\\\ z & =\\frac{-1\\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-12983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be85a13ae3e6705f279a18dfde732f4cf6b0db78f5c2d7309958788632fd3eec"} {"question" "q-12983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-12983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p+q=\\frac{11}{4},\\,z=\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{11}}{2}"] ["math" "p+q=\\frac{13}{4},\\,z=\\frac{-1\\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}"] ["math" "p+q=\\frac{15}{4},\\,z=\\frac{-1\\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}"] ["math" "p+q=\\frac{15}{4},\\,z=\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{11}}{2}"] ["math" "p+q=\\frac{17}{4},\\,z=\\frac{-3\\pm \\sqrt{11}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-12983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p+q=\\frac{15}{4},\\,z=\\frac{-1\\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation $-20{x}^{2}+60x-41=0$ can be written in the form $20(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q,$ and solve the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-20{x}^{2}+60x-41) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-60x+41 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{x}^{2}-60x+41 & =0 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-60x & =-41 \\\\ 20({x}^{2}-3x) & =-41 \\\\ 20[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}] & =-41 \\\\ 20[{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}] & =-41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-20\\cdot \\frac{9}{4} & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-45 & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =45-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q=4.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{20} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{3}{2}| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be85a13ae3e6705f279a18dfde732f4cf6b0db78f5c2d7309958788632fd3eec"} {"question" "q-60145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "q=2,\\,x=3\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] ["math" "q=2,\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "q=4,\\,x=2\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] ["math" "q=4,\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] ["math" "q=4,\\,x=\\frac{3}{4}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "q=4,\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation $2{x}^{2}+10x+12=0$ can be written in the form $2(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p,$ and solve the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side,  factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+10x+12 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+10x & =-12 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+10x & =-12 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+5x) & =-12 \\\\ 2[{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}] & =-12 \\\\ 2[{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{25}{4}] & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{25}{4} & =-12 \\\\ 2{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{25}{2} & =-12 \\\\ 2{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} & =-12+\\frac{25}{2} \\\\ 2{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{5}{2}.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\ |x+\\frac{5}{2}| & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x+\\frac{5}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{6}{3}=-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{4}{2}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-3$ and $x=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be85a13ae3e6705f279a18dfde732f4cf6b0db78f5c2d7309958788632fd3eec"} {"question" "q-60359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=\\frac{1}{2},\\,x=-2$ and $2$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{1}{2},\\,x=-3$ and $-2$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{5}{2},\\,x=-3$ and $-2$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{5}{2},\\,x=-4$ and $-3$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{5}{2},\\,x=3$ and $2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-60359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=\\frac{5}{2},\\,x=-3$ and $-2$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-86414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation $-3{x}^{2}+36x-94=0$ can be written in the form $3(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q-p.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-86414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}+36x-94) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-36x+94 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-36x+94 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-36x & =-94 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-12x] & =-94 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2}-{6}^{2}] & =-94 \\\\ 3[{(x-6)}^{2}-36] & =-94\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(x-6)}^{2}-3\\cdot 36 & =-94 \\\\ 3{(x-6)}^{2}-108 & =-94 \\\\ 3{(x-6)}^{2} & =-94+108 \\\\ 3{(x-6)}^{2} & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-6$, $q=14.$ Finally,\n\n$$\nq-p=14-(-6)=14+6=20.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-86414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be85a13ae3e6705f279a18dfde732f4cf6b0db78f5c2d7309958788632fd3eec"} {"question" "q-86414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-86414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "q-p=14"] ["math" "q-p=15"] ["math" "q-p=20"] ["math" "q-p=25"] ["math" "q-p=6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-86414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "q-p=20"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-112625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The equation $-4{w}^{2}-16w+9=0$ can be written in the form $4(w+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p,$ and solve the equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-112625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-4{w}^{2}-16w+9) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}+16w-9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{w}^{2}+16w-9 & =0 \\\\ 4{w}^{2}+16w & =9 \\\\ 4({w}^{2}+4w) & =9 \\\\ 4[{w}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot w+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}] & =9 \\\\ 4[{(w+2)}^{2}-4] & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w+2)}^{2}-4\\cdot 4 & =9 \\\\ 4{(w+2)}^{2}-16 & =9 \\\\ 4{(w+2)}^{2} & =9+16 \\\\ 4{(w+2)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=2.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(w+2)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {(w+2)}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(w+2)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\ |w+2| & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ w+2 & =\\pm \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ w & =-2\\pm \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =-2-\\frac{5}{2}=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ w & =-2+\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $w=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-112625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be85a13ae3e6705f279a18dfde732f4cf6b0db78f5c2d7309958788632fd3eec"} {"question" "q-112625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-112625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=1,\\,w=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "$p=1,\\,w=-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $w=1$"] ["text" "$p=2,\\,w=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{5}{2}$"] ["text" "$p=2,\\,w=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "$p=2,\\,w=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{1}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"} {"question" "q-112625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=2,\\,w=-\\frac{9}{2}$ and $w=\\frac{1}{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039622/state.json" "file_sha256" "e61a1124eb1973d75931f5afbe4a0993ae8037cd053a39db5956073ef2780788"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1370 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
